EXT. FLOODED TRENCH - DAWN

Mud to the knees. Barbed wire. Smoke on the horizon.

PRIVATE EMIL HARTMANN (20s, cracked glasses) crouches against the wall, rifle across his lap. A SOLDIER IN A TORN GREATCOAT (30s) slides into the trench beside him, breathing hard.

SOLDIER
Is this Third Company?

EMIL
Who's asking?

SOLDIER
Corporal. Lost my squad in the night.

EMIL
Name?

SOLDIER
Brandt. Franz Brandt.

EMIL
Then welcome, Corporal Brandt.

Brandt leans back against the mud.

BRANDT
Quiet this morning.

EMIL
Too quiet.

A whistle shrieks overhead. Both men duck. A shell lands a hundred yards off, throwing up a column of dirt. Silence. Then Emil laughs, shakily.

EMIL (CONT'D)
That was close.

BRANDT
Not close enough.

They sit in the mud. Neither speaks. The smoke drifts on.
